course: dictionary
lesson: 6012
title: Medical words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Medical is an adjective. It describes things to do with medicine, doctors, illness and keeping people healthy. «She needed medical help after the fall» means she needed a doctor or nurse, not just a plaster. Look at the words around it to check.
explain: In British English, medical can also be a noun: a medical is a check of your body by a doctor. «He had a medical before joining the team» tells you a doctor checked his health first. The clue is "before joining the team", which is the sort of time a check would happen.
explain: Other words to learn in this family are medical emergency, medical kit, medical bracelet and medical centre. A medical emergency is serious and needs help at once, so you call the emergency number.
explain: Some children wear a medical bracelet. It tells helpers about an allergy or illness, so they know how to help you safely if you cannot speak for yourself.
fact: Medical means to do with medicine, doctors, illness and keeping people healthy.
fact: A medical emergency needs help at once, so you call the emergency number.
fact: Heatstroke is a medical emergency, and one warning sign is that a hot person stops sweating.
fact: «A nosebleed that will not stop after 20 minutes» needs medical help.
fact: Long ago, Egyptian doctors set broken bones, stitched wounds and wrote medical books.
exercise: «A big burn needs an adult to call for medical help.» What does medical help mean? | * Help from doctors or nurses | Help from a friend with a ball | Help with your homework | A new pair of shoes
exercise: Sam packed a medical kit for the camp. What is a medical kit? | * A box of supplies for treating injuries and illness | Shoes for walking | A tent for sleeping | A bag full of snacks
exercise: Which of these needs medical help? | A grazed knee that is not bleeding | A nosebleed that stops in two minutes | * A nosebleed that will not stop after 20 minutes | A tidy bedroom
test: Why is heatstroke called a medical emergency? | It makes you sleepy for a day | * It is serious and needs help at once | It only happens in winter | It is a sort of sunny weather
test: In which sentence does medical mean a health check by a doctor? | Medical books are heavy. | A medical kit is in the car. | * Dad had a medical before the trip, and the doctor checked his heart. | The medical centre is open late.
exam: What is a medical bracelet for? | To pay for food | * To tell helpers about an allergy or illness | To be fashionable | To keep the time
